meta {
  name: Create or update rating
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/ratings
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "productId": "{{productId}}",
    "taste": 7.5,
    "comment": "Pretty good",
    "seedSlug": "wine"
  }
}

docs {
  Upsert the caller's rating for a product. Body takes `productId` (TICKET-P6-009, was `barcode`) —
  must be a UUID (400 otherwise). taste is a Float in [0, 10] on 0.5 increments.

  TICKET-P6-003 category fields — `categoryId` and `seedSlug` are optional and mutually exclusive:
  - Omit both: the rating's existing category (if any) is left UNTOUCHED. This is the safe default for
    a replayed/offline-queued request — it must never silently wipe a category assigned since the
    request was first queued.
  - `categoryId: "<uuid>"`: assign one of the caller's own categories (404 unknown id, 403 another
    user's).
  - `categoryId: null`: explicitly clear the category.
  - `seedSlug: "<slug>"`: find-or-create that seed category for the caller in the same request, then
    assign it — rating and categorising in one round trip. See List/Create category for the slug list.
  - Both `categoryId` and `seedSlug` together is 400 (ambiguous).

  Response:
  - 201 Created — first rating for this (user, product) pair
  - 200 OK — existing rating overwritten (same id, createdAt preserved, updatedAt advanced)
  - 404 — product not found (run Lookup product by GTIN first), or REJECTED; or an unknown categoryId
  - 403 — categoryId belongs to another user
  - 400 — validation error (missing fields, non-UUID productId, taste out of range, taste not on a 0.5
    boundary, bad category fields)
}
